# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Use KEY=value with no spaces around `=`.
#
# During /setup, Claude extends this file with the project's real variables
# (API URLs, publishable keys, service DSNs, …) and comments on where each
# value comes from.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Task Master AI (CLI/MCP) — ALL OPTIONAL with this template.
# .taskmaster/config.json uses the `claude-code` provider, which reuses your
# Claude Code session — no API key needed. Only add keys here if you switch to
# API-based models or want `--research` mode (Perplexity recommended for that).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-api03-..."
#PERPLEXITY_API_KEY="pplx-..."
#OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-proj-..."
#GOOGLE_API_KEY="..."
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY="..."

# ── Project variables
# None are needed until a venture reaches launch. Each is requested from the
# owner once, when the corresponding channel is set up.

# Merchant of record: Stripe Managed Payments (decided 2026-09-18; it replaced
# Lemon Squeezy for UK sellers). From: dashboard.stripe.com → Developers → API
# keys (restricted key: read checkout sessions, write nothing else) and
# Webhooks (signing secret). Used by @foundry/licensing to issue license keys
# on `checkout.session.completed`. Server-side only.
#STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
#STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Ed25519 private key that signs license keys; public half is embedded in
# products. Generated once by `npm run licensing:keygen` (task 3).
#LICENSE_SIGNING_KEY=""

# Telemetry collector (Cloudflare Worker). Write key embedded in products;
# read key used by report scripts. From: `wrangler secret` output at deploy.
#TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT="https://<worker>.workers.dev/collect"
#TELEMETRY_WRITE_KEY=""
#TELEMETRY_READ_KEY=""

# Cloudflare Pages/Workers deploys. From: dash.cloudflare.com → API Tokens
# (template "Edit Cloudflare Workers"). Only needed by deploy scripts.
#CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""
#CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""

# Chrome Web Store publish API (optional automation; manual upload works too).
# From: Google Cloud console OAuth client + one-time consent flow.
#CWS_CLIENT_ID=""
#CWS_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#CWS_REFRESH_TOKEN=""
